      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two novel chiral ionic liquids are synthesized as the chiral selector. Racemates of amines, amino alcohols, and amino acids could generate enantioselective precipitate with multicomponent self-assemblies under mild conditions. The approach allows for enantioseparation with good yields (79-94%) and excellent ee's (>95%)."},
